{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017sWKdisNCfANmpW8K1boE6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though the specific reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026 don't appear to be published yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Current Information Available:\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements:\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Related Guidance:\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines aren't yet published, you can reference ICML and NeurIPS's extensive guidance to reviewers, which CoRL's guidelines build on. The search results show that previous CoRL reviewer guidelines covered relevance (whether the paper addresses robot learning, applies learning-based methods, and is evaluated in simulation or on real robots).\n\nFor the most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you may want to check the official CoRL website or OpenReview page directly, as these documents may not yet be publicly available.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8217637-8c12-424b-9256-3d9dc7b16457","uuid":"6ec9ce83-8ccb-4c2c-99bb-945713105954","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:17:07.904Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GeL6uBFHWyBxCTP1kVXJB3","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though the specific reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026 don't appear to be published yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Current Information Available:\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements:\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Related Guidance:\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines aren't yet published, you can reference ICML and NeurIPS's extensive guidance to reviewers, which CoRL's guidelines build on. The search results show that previous CoRL reviewer guidelines covered relevance (whether the paper addresses robot learning, applies learning-based methods, and is evaluated in simulation or on real robots).\n\nFor the most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you may want to check the official CoRL website or OpenReview page directly, as these documents may not yet be publicly available."],"durationSeconds":5.350016370999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RwwLFzJHxt2Nx7FYZPbjbf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CommunityConnect 2025 Scoring Rubric for Abstracts 5 Excellent 4 Good 3 Fair 2\",\"url\":\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/9100a73e/files/uploaded/2025_Reviewer_Rating_Form_(Workshop_Rubric).pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found limited specific information about CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric. Here's what I was able to locate:\n\n**Current Status:**\nCoRL 2025 Conference is hosted on OpenReview, but the detailed reviewer guidelines, review form, and scoring rubric for 2025 were not directly available in the search results.\n\n**Related Information:**\nThe search returned reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023, which states that CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly, while obvious shortcomings not reported by authors should be pointed out extensively and reflected in scores.\n\nFor CoRL 2024, submissions were evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n**To Access the Official Documents:**\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric, I recommend:\n1. Visiting the OpenReview page directly at: https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Conference\n2. Checking the official CoRL website at www.corl.org\n3. Looking for any email communications from the conference organizers if you are already a registered reviewer\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8217637-8c12-424b-9256-3d9dc7b16457","uuid":"23a628b4-7c38-4dd7-aeda-c39ee6036c47","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:17:08.203Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Jt5KiHh26PvfrATvLLLtqR","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instru