{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W1Qbs8xQeHD8YHrneWugLe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORLcleared Vendor Scoring Process – CORL_Portal\",\"url\":\"https://corl-portal.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/14440881933339-CORLcleared-Vendor-Scoring-Process\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024\"},{\"title\":\"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up\",\"url\":\"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 review instructions. Here's what the scoring and rating criteria include:\n\n## Review Criteria for CoRL 2024\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nThe process includes evaluation for potential desk rejection. The paper can be desk rejected for one of the three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. Specifically regarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate the relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\n## Review Process Guidelines\n\nWhile the search results provide some reviewer guidance from CoRL 2023 (which may be similar to 2024), they indicate that obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in your scores.\n\nFor more detailed information about the specific numeric scoring scale and rating criteria used for CoRL 2024 reviews, you may need to access the full instruction for reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews, as the search results only showed partial content from that page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8217637-8c12-424b-9256-3d9dc7b16457","uuid":"25f4ad7c-6977-4f49-a32b-05401c775f3d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:17:21.601Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011Xr5yz8JkoQWgNsk3f87qb","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CORLcleared Vendor Scoring Process – CORL_Portal","url":"https://corl-portal.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/14440881933339-CORLcleared-Vendor-Scoring-Process"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference"},{"title":"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024"},{"title":"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up","url":"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/"},{"title":"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery","url":"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 review instructions. Here's what the scoring and rating criteria include:\n\n## Review Criteria for CoRL 2024\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nThe process includes evaluation for potential desk rejection. The paper can be desk rejected for one of the three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. Specifically regarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate the relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\n## Review Process Guidelines\n\nWhile the search results provide some reviewer guidance from CoRL 2023 (which may be similar to 2024), they indicate that obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in your scores.\n\nFor more detailed information about the specific numeric scoring scale and rating criteria used for CoRL 2024 reviews, you may need to access the full instruction for reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews, as the search results only showed partial content from that page."],"durationSeconds":5.453667485999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qszQUMeBwGVuDzpqKQWDF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric rating scale accept reject\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"},{\"title\":\"Conference on Robot Learning\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/corl_conf/status/1666663426339508224\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here's what the scoring rubric covers:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nThe main review part asks for an evaluation of originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work. The guidelines elaborate on each criterion:\n\n**Originality:** The guidelines ask whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques (which can be valuable), if it's clear how the work differs from previous contributions, and if related work is adequately cited.\n\n**Quality:** Quality assessment focuses on whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, if methods are appropriate, if it's a complete work or work in progress, and if authors are careful and honest about evaluating strengths and weaknesses.\n\n**Clarity:** The clarity criteria evaluate whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n## Review Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores. Reviewers are asked to be constructive, concrete, courteous and respectful.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain the specific numerical rating scale (e.g., 1-5 scale) or the specific accept/reject thresholds used by CoRL 2023.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8217637-8c12-424b-9256-3d9dc7b16457","uuid":"461141e7-8c9f-43dd-88b7-dde7e0801253","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:17:26.300Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric rating scale accept reject","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015jovEGfSdBygqGKTZLGwsc","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference"},{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/"},{"title":"Conference on Robot Learning","url":"https://twitter.com/corl_conf/status/1666663426339508224"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here's what the scoring rubric covers:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nThe main review part asks for an evaluation of originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work. The guidelines elaborate on each criterion:\n\n**Originality:** The guidelines ask whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques (which can be valuable), if it's clear how the work differs from previous contributions, and if related work is adequately cited.\n\n**Quality:** Quality assessment focuses on whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, if methods are appropriate, if it's a complete work or work in progress, and if authors are careful and honest about evaluating strengths and weaknesses.\n\n**Clarity:** The clarity criteria evaluate whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n## Review Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores. Reviewers are asked to be constructive, concrete, courteous and respectful.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain the specific numerical rating scale (e.g., 1-5 scale) or the specific accept/reject thresholds used by CoRL 2023."],"durationSeconds":9.695275526999998}}
